  "history_summaries": [
    "Round 1/3 — DUT bug fix (alternative to unavailable fvAssume). Added validPegs guard (io.from <= 2.U && io.to <= 2.U) to the disc-update conditional: when(legal && validPegs). This prevents discs from being assigned invalid peg 3 when the formal solver drives io.from/io.to to 3, breaking the causal chain that violated all 20 disc_*_on_valid_peg assertions. The fix addresses the causal path (disc update firing on invalid input pegs) rather than only the observed waveform symptom. All existing assertions are preserved unchanged. Target assertion: disc_0_on_valid_peg.",
    "Round 2/3 — Assertion fix (assertion_error) for disc_moved_to_destination. Root cause: RegNext registers (legalPrev, sizeFromPrev, toPrev) have unconstrained initial values in the formal model; the solver picks legalPrev=1, sizeFromPrev=31 (out-of-bounds), toPrev=3 causing disc(31%20=11)=0 !== 3 → assertion fails. Fix: added prevValid = RegInit(false.B) guard that suppresses the assertion on the first cycle before the RegNext registers have been clocked. The assertion label is preserved exactly. No homologous assertions exist (only one assertion uses this RegNext pattern). The remaining from_valid_peg and to_valid_peg failures are separate issues to be addressed in round 3.",
    "Round 3/3 — Assertion fix (assertion_error) for disc_moved_to_destination. Root cause: the assertion antecedent only checked legalPrev but the disc-update path is guarded by legal && validPegs (added in round 1). When the formal solver assigns io.to=3 (invalid peg), validPegs is false, so the disc is never updated, yet the assertion expects disc(sizeFromPrev)===toPrev, causing a counterexample. The fix adds validPegsPrev=RegNext(validPegs) and includes !validPegsPrev in the antecedent, making the antecedent (!prevValid || !legalPrev || !validPegsPrev) match the update guard (legal && validPegs). The assertion label disc_moved_to_destination is preserved exactly. Simple `RegNext` temporal sampling captures validPegs from the antecedent cycle. No structurally identical assertions exist (this is the only assertion using this RegNext pattern). Remaining from_valid_peg and to_valid_peg failures are about raw input validity constraints (cannot be fixed with fvAssume as it's unavailable)."
  ],
